A uniform beam $AB$ of length $6.0\text{ m}$ is placed on a horizontal surface and then tilted at an angle of $31^{\circ}$ to the horizontal, as shown in Fig. 2.1.

{{figure:figure_2_1.png}}

The beam is held in equilibrium by four forces that all act in the same plane. A force of $90\text{ N}$ acts perpendicular to the beam at end $A$. The weight $W$ of the beam acts at its centre of gravity. A vertical force $Y$ and a horizontal force $X$ both act at end $B$ of the beam.
